[258.59482, "o", "/app/audit-extractor/src/parser/corrections.js:2:  const start = markdown.indexOf(\"## Correction Notices\");\r\r\n/app/audit-extractor/src/parser/corrections.js:3:  const end = markdown.indexOf(\"## Transaction Ledger\");\r\r\n/app/audit-extractor/src/parser/emails.js:2:  const start = markdown.indexOf(\"## Email Excerpts\");\r\r\n/app/audit-extractor/src/parser/emails.js:3:  const end = markdown.indexOf(\"## Policy Exceptions\");\r\r\n/app/audit-extractor/src/parser/ledger.js:2:  const start = markdown.indexOf(\"## Transaction Ledger\");\r\r\n/app/audit-extractor/src/parser/policy.js:2:  const start = markdown.indexOf(\"## Policy Exceptions\");\r\r\n/app/audit-extractor/src/parser/policy.js:3:  const end = markdown.indexOf(\"## Correction Notices\");\r\r\n"]
[258.595555, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@3f2a24e5dabd:/app# "]
[259.598911, "i", "sed -n '1,260p' /app/audit-extractor/src/parser/sections.js | head -n 80\n"]
[259.600302, "o", "sed -n '1,260p' /app/audit-extractor/src/parser/sections.js | head -n 80"]
[259.601625, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[259.606655, "o", "const { parseLedger } = require(\"./ledger\");\r\r\nconst { parseMeetings } = require(\"./meetings\");\r\r\nconst { parseEmails } = require(\"./emails\");\r\r\nconst { parseCorrections } = require(\"./corrections\");\r\r\nconst { parsePolicyExceptions } = require(\"./policy\");\r\r\n\r\r\nfunction parseArchive(markdown) {\r\r\n  return {\r\r\n    ledger: parseLedger(markdown),\r\r\n    meetings: parseMeetings(markdown),\r\r\n    emails: parseEmails(markdown),\r\r\n    corrections: parseCorrections(markdown),\r\r\n    policyExceptions: parsePolicyExceptions(markdown),\r\r\n  };\r\r\n}\r\r\n\r\r\nmodule.exports = { parseArchive };\r\r\n"]
[259.608996, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@3f2a24e5dabd:/app# "]
[270.12292, "i", "for b in 02 03 04 06 07 08; do echo \"\\n===== BRIEF $b (binding section) =====\"; start=$(grep -n \"^## Investigation Brief $b\" /app/data/audit_archive.md | head -n1 | cut -d: -f1); end=$(grep -n \"^## Investigation Brief $b .*— field notes\" /app/data/audit_archive.md | head -n1 | cut -d: -f1); if [ -n \"$start\" ] && [ -n \"$end\" ]; then sed -n \"${start},$((end-1))p\" /app/data/audit_archive.md; else echo \"missing range $b start=$start end=$end\"; fi; done\n"]
[270.129944, "o", "for b in 02 03 04 06 07 08; do echo \"\\n===== BRIEF $b (binding section) =====\"; start=$(grep -n \"^## Investigation Brief $b\" /app/data/audit_archive.md | head -n1 | cut -d: -f1); end=$(grep -n \"^## Investigation Brief $b .*— field notes\" /app/data/audit_archive.md | head -n1 | cut -d: -f1); if [ -n \"$start\" ] && [ -n \"$end\" ]; then sed -n \"${start},$((end-1))p\" /app/data/audit_archive.md; else echo \"missing range $b start=$start end=$end\"; fi; done\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[270.130801, "o", "\\n===== BRIEF 02 (binding section) =====\r\n"]
[270.148402, "o", "## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence\r\n\r\nAuditor directive (mandatory for extract):\r\n\r\nInterview notes with the compliance desk confirmed status fights between mail,\r\namendments, and corrections. Ledger rows provide the base status (lowercase on\r\noutput). Status precedence from lowest to highest is: pending, approved,\r\nrejected, reversed. Email excerpts may change status only when the From line\r\ncontains `compliance@` anywhere in the address; ignore all other senders.\r\n\r\n"]
[270.150192, "o", "\\n===== BRIEF 03 (binding section) =====\r\n"]
[270.165656, "o", "## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing\r\n"]
[270.166341, "o", "\r\nExtract policy (authoritative):\r\n\r\nThe March mail-room audit explained missing holds: agents applied compliance\r\nmessages without checking dispatch dates. When an excerpt includes\r\n`sent: YYYY-MM-DD`, apply the status change only if sent is greater than or\r\nequal to the ledger date for that transaction. When no `sent:` line is present,\r\napply the status change if precedence allows. Correction notices always apply\r\nafter ledger rows, meeting amendments, and mail excerpts have been merged.\r\n\r\n"]
[270.166838, "o", "\\n===== BRIEF 04 (binding section) =====\r\n"]
[270.194494, "o", "## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence\r\n"]
[270.195466, "o", "\r\nController memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n\r\nThe corrections desk ships multiple notices per field. When several notices\r\ntarget the same transaction and field, the notice with the lexicographically\r\ngreatest `effective` date wins. For each winning notice, `previous_value` in\r\n`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is the field value immediately before that notice\r\napplies (after ledger, amendments, and emails). Owner corrections override\r\nboth ledger owners and signed meeting amendments when applied in this step.\r\n\r\n"]
[270.195796, "o", "\\n===== BRIEF 06 (binding section) =====\r\n"]
[270.213798, "o", "## Investigation Brief 06 — Effective Dates on Output\r\n\r\nAuditor directive (mandatory for extract):\r\n\r\nAuditors compared effective_date columns to correction paperwork. Start from the\r\nledger `date` field (YYYY-MM-DD on output). When a winning correction notice\r\nsets field `date` or `status`, use that notice's `effective` date as\r\n`effective_date` only if that correction modified status or date; otherwise\r\nkeep the ledger date. `amount_usd` is numeric from the ledger with two decimal\r\nplaces in CSV and as a JSON number.\r\n\r\n\\n===== BRIEF 07 (binding section) =====\r\n"]
[270.240054, "o", "## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I)\r\n\r\nExtract policy (authoritative):\r\n\r\nException coding review: `exception_reason` is null unless a code applies. Set\r\n`over_limit` when `amount_usd` strictly exceeds 10000. Set `compliance_hold`\r\nwhen final status is `rejected`, a qualifying `compliance@` email referenced\r\nthat transaction, and that email block includes a `sent:` line. The sent-date\r\ncomparison used for `compliance_hold` is defined in Investigation Brief 09\r\n(Mid-Year Amendment), not Brief 03. Multiple reasons join with semicolon in\r\nlexical order of the reason codes.\r\n\r\n"]
[270.241387, "o", "\\n===== BRIEF 08 (binding section) =====\r\n"]
[270.260904, "o", "## Investigation Brief 08 — Exception Flags (Part II) and Artifacts\r\n"]
[270.261518, "o", "\r\n"]
[270.261738, "o", "Controller memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n\r\nContinued from Brief 07. Set `policy_waiver` when final status is `approved`,\r\n`amount_usd` > 10000, and a Policy Exception block exists for that transaction\r\nwith `approved_by: compliance` on its own line. Set `retroactive_review` when\r\nfinal status is `reversed`, `amount_usd` > 5000, and a winning correction\r\nnotice changed status for that transaction.\r\n"]
[270.262253, "o", "\r\n`extract --outdir` must write: `transactions.json` as `{\"items\":[...]}` sorted\r\nby `transaction_id` ascending with fields transaction_id, owner, status\r\n(lowercase), effective_date, amount_usd, exception_reason (null or\r\nsemicolon-joined codes). `transactions.csv` uses header\r\ntransaction_id,owner,status,effective_date,amount_usd,exception_reason with the\r\nsame rows; leave exception_reason blank when null. `exceptions.json` is\r\n`{\"items\":[...]}` with only rows where exception_reason is set.\r\n`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is one JSON object per winning correction with\r\nnotice_id, transaction_id, field, previous_value, new_value, effective, sorted\r\nby notice_id ascending.\r\n\r\n"]
[270.263797, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@3f2a24e5dabd:/app# "]
[271.127306, "i", "sed -n '1,220p' /app/audit-extractor/src/parser/ledger.js\n"]
[271.127822, "o", "sed -n '1,220p' /app/audit-extractor/src/parser/ledger.js\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[271.1367, "o", "function parseLedger(markdown) {\r\r\n  const start = markdown.indexOf(\"## Transaction Ledger\");\r\r\n  if (start < 0) {\r\r\n    return [];\r\r\n  }\r\r\n  const slice = markdown.slice(start);\r\r\n  const rows = [];\r\r\n  const blocks = slice.split(/^### /m).slice(1);\r\r\n  for (const block of blocks) {\r\r\n    const lines = block.split(\"\\n\");\r\r\n    const transactionId = lines[0].trim();\r\r\n    if (!transactionId.startsWith(\"TXN-\")) {\r\r\n      continue;\r\r\n    }\r\r\n    if (rows.some((row) => row.transaction_id === transactionId)) {\r\r\n      continue;\r\r\n    }\r\r\n    const row = { transaction_id: transactionId };\r\r\n    for (const line of lines) {\r\r\n      const trimmed = line.trim();\r\r\n      if (trimmed.startsWith(\"amount:\")) {\r\r\n        row.amount = Number(trimmed.split(\":\")[1].trim());\r\r\n      } else if (trimmed.startsWith(\"owner:\")) {\r\r\n        row.owner = trimmed.split(\":\")[1].trim();\r\r\n      } else if (trimmed.startsWith(\"status:\")) {\r\r\n        row.status = trimmed.split(\":\")[1].trim();\r\r\n      } else if (trimmed.startsWith(\"date:\")) "]
[271.138532, "o", "{\r\r\n        row.date = trimmed.split(\":\")[1].trim();\r\r\n      }\r\r\n    }\r\r\n    rows.push(row);\r\r\n  }\r\r\n  return rows;\r\r\n}\r\r\n\r\r\nmodule.exports = { parseLedger };\r\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@3f2a24e5dabd:/app# "]
[271.52168, "i", "sed -n '1,220p' /app/audit-extractor/src/parser/corrections.js\n"]
[271.52177, "o", "sed -n '1,220p' /app/audit-extractor/src/parser/corrections.js\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[271.526145, "o", "function parseCorrections(markdown) {\r\r\n  const start = markdown.indexOf(\"## Correction Notices\");\r\r\n  const end = markdown.indexOf(\"## Transaction Ledger\");\r\r\n  const slice =\r\r\n    start >= 0 && end > start ? markdown.slice(start, end) : \"\";\r\r\n  const notices = [];\r\r\n  const blocks = slice.split(/^### /m).slice(1);\r\r\n  for (const block of blocks) {\r\r\n    const lines = block.split(\"\\n\");\r\r\n    const noticeId = lines[0].trim();\r\r\n    if (!noticeId.startsWith(\"CORR-\")) {\r\r\n      continue;\r\r\n    }\r\r\n    const entry = { notice_id: noticeId };\r\r\n    for (const line of lines) {\r\r\n      const trimmed = line.trim();\r\r\n      if (trimmed.startsWith(\"targets:\")) {\r\r\n        entry.transaction_id = trimmed.split(\":\")[1].trim();\r\r\n      } else if (trimmed.startsWith(\"field:\")) {\r\r\n        entry.field = trimmed.split(\":\")[1].trim();\r\r\n      } else if (trimmed.startsWith(\"value:\")) {\r\r\n        entry.value = trimmed.split(\":\")[1].trim();\r\r\n      } else if (trimmed.startsWith(\"effective:\")) {\r\r\n        entry.effective = trimme"]
[271.526287, "o", "d.split(\":\")[1].trim();\r\r\n      }\r\r\n    }\r\r\n    notices.push(entry);\r\r\n  }\r\r\n  return notices;\r\r\n}\r\r\n\r\r\nmodule.exports = { parseCorrections };\r\r\n"]
[271.526688, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[271.528312, "o", "root@3f2a24e5dabd:/app# "]
[271.912984, "i", "sed -n '1,220p' /app/audit-extractor/src/parser/policy.js\n"]
[271.913391, "o", "sed -n '1,220p' /app/audit-extractor/src/parser/policy.js\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[271.921958, "o", "function parsePolicyExceptions(markdown) {\r\r\n"]
[271.922624, "o", "  const start = markdown.indexOf(\"## Policy Exceptions\");\r\r\n"]
[271.922644, "o", "  const end = markdown.indexOf(\"## Correction Notices\");\r\r\n  const slice =\r\r\n    start >= 0 && end > start ? markdown.slice(start, end) : \"\";\r\r\n  const ids = new Set();\r\r\n  const re = /^transaction:\\s*(TXN-[0-9a-f-]+)\\s*$/gim;\r\r\n  let match;\r\r\n  while ((match = re.exec(slice)) !== null) {\r\r\n    ids.add(match[1]);\r\r\n  }\r\r\n  return ids;\r\r\n}\r\r\n\r\r\nmodule.exports = { parsePolicyExceptions };\r\r\n"]
[271.923411, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@3f2a24e5dabd:/app# "]
[282.145616, "i", "for b in 02 03 04 06 07 08; do start=$(grep -n \"^## Investigation Brief $b\" /app/data/audit_archive.md | head -n1 | cut -d: -f1); end=$(grep -n \"^## Investigation Brief $b .*— field notes\" /app/data/audit_archive.md | head -n1 | cut -d: -f1); out=/tmp/binding-brief${b}.md; if [ -n \"$start\" ] && [ -n \"$end\" ]; then sed -n \"${start},$((end-1))p\" /app/data/audit_archive.md > \"$out\"; else echo \"missing range $b start=$start end=$end\" > \"$out\"; fi; done\n"]
[282.14863, "o", "for b in 02 03 04 06 07 08; do start=$(grep -n \"^## Investigation Brief $b\" /app/data/audit_archive.md | head -n1 | cut -d: -f1); end=$(grep -n \"^## Investigation Brief $b .*— field notes\" /app/data/audit_archive.md | head -n1 | cut -d: -f1); out=/tmp/binding-brief${b}.md; if [ -n \"$start\" ] && [ -n \"$end\" ]; then sed -n \"${start},$((end-1))p\" /app/data/audit_archive.md > \"$out\"; else echo \"missing range $b start=$start end=$end\" > \"$out\"; fi; done"]
[282.149387, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[282.203588, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@3f2a24e5dabd:/app# "]
[283.287959, "i", "for f in /tmp/binding-brief0{2,3,4,6,7,8}.md; do echo \"\\n===== $f =====\"; sed -n '1,160p' \"$f\"; done\n"]
[283.288926, "o", "for f in /tmp/binding-brief0{2,3,4,6,7,8}.md; do echo \"\\n===== $f =====\"; sed -n '1,160p' \"$f\"; done\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\\n===== /tmp/binding-brief02.md =====\r\n"]
[283.297559, "o", "## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence\r\n\r\n"]
[283.298241, "o", "Auditor directive (mandatory for extract):\r\n\r\nInterview notes with the compliance desk confirmed status fights between mail,\r\namendments, and corrections. Ledger rows provide the base status (lowercase on\r\noutput). Status precedence from lowest to highest is: pending, approved,\r\nrejected, reversed. Email excerpts may change status only when the From line\r\ncontains `compliance@` anywhere in the address; ignore all other senders.\r\n\r\n\\n===== /tmp/binding-brief03.md =====\r\n"]
[283.300872, "o", "## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing\r\n\r\nExtract policy (authoritative):\r\n\r\nThe March mail-room audit explained missing holds: agents applied compliance\r\nmessages without checking dispatch dates. When an excerpt includes\r\n`sent: YYYY-MM-DD`, apply the status change only if sent is greater than or\r\nequal to the ledger date for that transaction. When no `sent:` line is present,\r\napply the status change if precedence allows. Correction notices always apply\r\nafter ledger rows, meeting amendments, and mail excerpts have been merged.\r\n\r\n\\n===== /tmp/binding-brief04.md =====\r\n"]
[283.30323, "o", "## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence\r\n\r\nController memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n\r\nThe corrections desk ships multiple notices per field. When several notices\r\ntarget the same transaction and field, the notice with the lexicographically\r\ngreatest `effective` date wins. For each winning notice, `previous_value` in\r\n`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is the field value immediately before that notice\r\napplies (after ledger, amendments, and emails). Owner corrections override\r\nboth ledger owners and signed meeting amendments when applied in this step.\r\n\r\n"]
[283.303344, "o", "\\n===== /tmp/binding-brief06.md =====\r\n"]
[283.30597, "o", "## Investigation Brief 06 — Effective Dates on Output\r\n\r\nAuditor directive (mandatory for extract):\r\n\r\nAuditors compared effective_date columns to correction paperwork. Start from the\r\nledger `date` field (YYYY-MM-DD on output). When a winning correction notice\r\nsets field `date` or `status`, use that notice's `effective` date as\r\n`effective_date` only if that correction modified status or date; otherwise\r\nkeep the ledger date. `amount_usd` is numeric from the ledger with two decimal\r\nplaces in CSV and as a JSON number.\r\n\r\n"]
[283.30626, "o", "\\n===== /tmp/binding-brief07.md =====\r\n"]
[283.308811, "o", "## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I)\r\n\r\nExtract policy (authoritative):\r\n\r\nException coding review: `exception_reason` is null unless a code applies. Set\r\n`over_limit` when `amount_usd` strictly exceeds 10000. Set `compliance_hold`\r\nwhen final status is `rejected`, a qualifying `compliance@` email referenced\r\nthat transaction, and that email block includes a `sent:` line. The sent-date\r\ncomparison used for `compliance_hold` is defined in Investigation Brief 09\r\n(Mid-Year Amendment), not Brief 03. Multiple reasons join with semicolon in\r\nlexical order of the reason codes.\r\n\r\n"]
[283.308937, "o", "\\n===== /tmp/binding-brief08.md =====\r\n"]
[283.311543, "o", "## Investigation Brief 08 — Exception Flags (Part II) and Artifacts\r\n\r\nController memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n\r\nContinued from Brief 07. Set `policy_waiver` when final status is `approved`,\r\n`amount_usd` > 10000, and a Policy Exception block exists for that transaction\r\nwith `approved_by: compliance` on its own line. Set `retroactive_review` when\r\nfinal status is `reversed`, `amount_usd` > 5000, and a winning correction\r\nnotice changed status for that transaction.\r\n\r\n`extract --outdir` must write: `transactions.json` as `{\"items\":[...]}` sorted\r\nby `transaction_id` ascending with fields transaction_id, owner, status\r\n(lowercase), effective_date, amount_usd, exception_reason (null or\r\n"]
[283.311728, "o", "semicolon-joined codes). `transactions.csv` uses header\r\ntransaction_id,owner,status,effective_date,amount_usd,exception_reason with the\r\nsame rows; leave exception_reason blank when null. `exceptions.json` is\r\n`{\"items\":[...]}` with only rows where exception_reason is set.\r\n`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is one JSON object per winning correction with\r\nnotice_id, transaction_id, field, previous_value, new_value, effective, sorted\r\nby notice_id ascending.\r\n\r\n\u001b[?2004h"]
[283.31212, "o", "root@3f2a24e5dabd:/app# "]
